hadiths[62]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4149","It was narrated that 'Ubadah bin As-Samit said:\We pledged to the Messenger of Allah to hear and obey"," both in times of ease and hardship"," when we felt energetic and when we felt tired"," that we would not contend with the orders of whomever was entrusted with it"," that we would was entrusted with it"," that we would stand firm in the way of truth wherever we may be"," and that we would not fear the blame of the blamers.\"""""
"4150","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""You have to obey when you feel energetic and when you feel tired"""
"4151","It was narrated that Jarir said:\\""I pledged to the Messenger of Allah to be sincere toward ever Muslim"""
"4152","Jarir said:\\""I pledged to the Prophet to hear and obey and to be sincere toward every Muslim"""
"4153","Jabir said:\\""We did not give our pledge to the Messenger of Allah for death"""
"4154","It was narrated that Yazid bin Abi 'Ubaid said:\\""I said to Salamah bin Al-Akwa': 'What pledge did you make to the Prophet on the Day of Al-Hudaibiyyah?' He said: 'For death"""
"4155","It was narrated that Ya'la bin Umayyah said:\\""I came to the Messenger of Allah with my father Umayyah on the Day of the Conquest (of Makkah) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"""
"4156","It was narrated that 'Ubadah bin As-Samit said:\\""While there was a group of his companions around him"""
"4157","It was narrated from 'Ubadah bin As-Samit that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""Why don't you pledge to me upon that which the women have pledged: That you will not associate anything with Allah"""
"4158","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr that a man came to the Prophet and said:\\""I have come pledging to emigrate (Hijrah)"""
"4159","It was narrated from Abu Sa'eed that:a Bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah about emigration (Hijrah). He said: \\""Woe to you"""
"4160","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Amr said:\\""A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Which emigration (Hijrah) is best?' He said: 'To leave what your Lord"""
"4161","It was narrated that Jabir bin Zaid said:\\""Ibn 'Abbas said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"4162","It was narrated from Kathir bin Murrah that Abu Fatimah told him that he said:\\""O Messenger of Allah"""
"4163","It was narrated from 'Amr bin 'Abdur-Rahman bin Umayyah that his father told him that Ya'la said:\\""I came to the Messenger of Allah with my father on the day of the Conquest (of Makkah) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"""
"4164","It was narrated that Safwan bin Umayyah said:\\""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"""
"4165","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said on the Day of the Conquest (of Makkah): \""\""There is no more emigration (Hijrah)"""
"4166","It was narrated that Nu'aim bin Dijajah said:\\""I heard 'Umar bin Al-Khattab say: 'There is no more emigration (Hijrah) after the death of the Messenger of Allah"""
"4167","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin Waqdan As-Sa'di said:\\""We came in a delegation to the messenger of Allah"""
"4168","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin As-Sa'di said:\\""We came in a delegation to the Messenger of Allah and my companions entered and asked their questions. I was the last of them to enter"""
"4169","Jarir said:\\""I came to the Prophet and said to him: 'I pledge to you to hear and obey in what I like and what I dislike.' The Prophet said: 'Can you do that"""
"4170","It was narrated that Jarir said:I pledged to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to perform Salah"
"4171","It was narrated that Jarir said:\\""I came to the Messenger of Allah\""\"" and he mentioned something similar"""
"4172","Jarir said:\\""I came to the Prophet when he was accepting (the people's) pledge"""
"4173","It was narrated that Abu Idris Al-Khawlani said:\\""I heard 'Ubadah bin As-Samit say: 'I pledged to the Messenger of Allah among a group of people"""
"4174","It was narrated that Umm 'Atiyyah said:\\""When I wanted to give pledge to the Messenger of Allah"""
"4175","It was narrated that Umm 'Atiyyah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah accepted our pledge that we would not wail (for the dead)"""
"4176","It was narrated that Umaimah bint Ruqaiqah said:\\""I came to the Prophet with some other Ansari women to give our pledge. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah"""
"4177","Jarir said: \I came to the Prophet when he was accepting (the people's) pledge"," and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," extend you hand so that I may give you my pledge"," and state your terms"," for you know best.' He said: 'I accept you pledge that you will worship Allah"," establish Salah"," pay the Zakah"," be sincere toward the Muslims"," and forsake the idolaters.\"""""
"4178","It was narrated that Al-Hirmas bin Ziyad said:\\""I stretched forth my hand to the Prophet for him to accept my pledge"""
"4179","It was narrated that jabir said:\\""A slave came and pledged to the Prophet to emigrate"""
"4180","It was narrated from Jabir bin 'Abdullah that:a Bedouin pledged Islam to the Messenger of Allah"
"4181","It was narrated from Salamah bin Al-Akwa ' that he entered upon Al-Hajjaj who said:O son of Al-Akwa"
"4182","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""We used to pledge to the Messenger of Allah to hear and obey"""
"4183","Ibn 'Umar said:\\""When we gave our pledge to the Messenger of Allah to hear and obey"""
"4184","It was narrated that Jarir bin 'Abdullah said:\\""I gave my pledge to the Prophet to hear and obey"""
"4185","It was narrated that Umaimah bin Ruqaiqah said:\\""We gave pledge to the Messenger of Allah among a group of women"""
"4186","It was narrated that 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Abd Rabb Al-Kabah said:\\"" I came to 'Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As while he was sitting in the shade of Kabah"""
"4187","It was narrated that Yahya bin Husain said:\\""I heard my grandmother say: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah say"""
"4188","Abu Hurairah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever obeys me"""
"4189","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas (concerning the Verse):\\""O you who believe! Obey Allah and obey the Messenger (Muhammad). That he said: This was revealed concerning 'Abdullah bin Hudhaifah bin Qais bin 'Adiyy"""
"4190","It was narrated from Muadah bin Jabal that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""Military campaigns are of two types: as for the one who seeks the Face of Allah"""
"4191","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""The Imam is like a shield whose orders should be obeyed when they (the Muslims) fight"""
"4192","It was narrated that Tamim Ad-Dari said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Religion is sincerity (An-Nasihah).' They said: 'To whom"""
"4193","It was narrated that Tamim Ad-Dari said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Religion is sincerity (An-Nasihah).' They said: 'To whom"""
"4194","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""Religion is sincerity"""
"4195","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""Religion is sincerity (An-Nasihah).\""\"" The said: \""\""To whom"""
"4196","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said \\"" The Messenger of Allah said:'No ruler is appointed but he has tow groups of advisers: A group which urges him to do good and tells him not to do evil"""
"4197","It was narrated from Abu Saeed tht the Messenger of Allah said:\\""Allah never sends a prophet or appoints a Khalifah but he has two groups of advisers: A group that tells him to do good and a group that tells him to do evil and urges him to do it. And the one who is truly protected is the one who is protected by Allah"""
"4198","It was narrated that Abu Ayyub said; \\""I heard the Messenger of Allah say:'No prophet has eve been sent"""
"4199","It was narrated that Al-Qasim bin Muhammad said:\\"" I heard my paternal aunt say: 'The Messenger of Allah said; \""\""Whoever among you is appointed to a position of authority. If Allah wills good for him. He will give him a righteous minister who will remind him if he forgets and help him if he remembers"""
"4200","It was narrated from Abu 'Adur-Rahman from Ali that:the Messenger of Allah sent an army and appointed a man in charge of them. He lit a fire and said: \\""Enter it.\""\"" Some people wanted to enter it"""
"4201","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'The Muslim must hear and obey whether he likes it or not"""
"4202","It was narrated that Kab bin Ujrah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah came out to us"""
"4203","It was narrated that Kab bin Ujrah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah came out to us and we were nine"""
"4204","It was narrated from Tariq bin Shihab that:a man asked the Prophet"
"4205","It was narrated that 'Ubadah bin As-Samit said:\\""We were with the Prophet in a gathering and he said: 'Pledge to me that you will not associate anything with Allah"""
"4206","it was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet said:\\""You will become keen for positions of authority"""
"4207","It was narrated that Kab bin Ujrah said:\The Messenger of Allah came out to us"," and there were nine of us. He said; 'After me there will be rulers"," whoever believes in their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me"," and I am not of him"," and he will not come to me at the Cistern. Whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their wrongdoing"," he is of me"," and I am of hi"," and he will come to me at the Cistern.\""'"""
"4208","It was narrated that Kab bin Ujrah said:\The Messenger of Allah came out to us and we were nine"," fie and four"," some 'Arabs and some non- 'Arabs. He said: 'Listen. Have you heard that after me there will be rulers"," whoever enters upon them and believes their lies and help them in their wrongdoing is not of me"," and I am not of him"," and he will not come to me at the Cistern? Whoever does not enter upon them or belive their lies or help them in their wrongdoing is of me and I am of him"," and he will come to me at the Cistern.\""'"""
"4210","it was narrated from Um Kurz that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""for a boy two sheep"""
"4211","It was narrated from Umm Kurz that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""For a boy two sheep"""
